No issues to report but I've noticed something while averaging segmented home ranges and wanted to ask you about it. So I've noticed each of the home range subsets I partition out usually result in an elliptical UD. Perhaps this is due to my rather coarse monitoring schedule compared to what many others are doing. Anyhow, when I go through the usual model selection route for each subset individually, it results in a UD that conforms more closely to the individual's locations than when the subsets are averaged together. For individual #155, I included the mean UD that is averaged over two subsets (Figure 1) and what the UD of each location cluster looks like when analyzed individually (Figures 2 and 3).

In situations like this when the home range segments do not overlap, would it be acceptable to analyze the segments individually and consider the cumulative area of both UDs as the annual home range?

Reagrds,
Ross

